#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:2
msgid "CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/include/ENV_VAR.rst:1
msgid ""
"This is a CMake :ref:`Environment Variable <CMake Language Environment "
"Variables>`. Its initial value is taken from the calling process environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:8
msgid "Record coverage of CMake language code in lcov tracefiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:10
msgid ""
"When this environment variable is set to a directory, each CMake process "
"that runs CMake language code records which lines of each listfile ran, and "
"how many times each function and macro was called.  At exit the process "
"writes this data into the directory.  This variable alone turns coverage "
"on.  There is no command-line option for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:16
msgid ""
"The value must be an absolute path.  If the directory does not exist, CMake "
"creates it.  If the variable is not set, or is set to an empty value, "
"coverage is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:20
msgid ""
"Child processes inherit the variable, so a :program:`cmake` process that a "
"project starts with :command:`execute_process` also records coverage.  On "
"every platform, this form sets the variable for one command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:24
msgid ""
"$ cmake -E env CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR=/path/to/dir cmake -S src -B build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:29
msgid "Modes that Record Coverage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:31
msgid "These modes record coverage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:33
msgid ""
"Configure and generate a project.  This includes projects "
"that :command:`try_compile` and :command:`try_run` configure, which record "
"into the same file as the parent project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:36
msgid "Script mode, :option:`cmake -P`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:37
msgid "Install scripts, :option:`cmake --install`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:38
msgid "A re-run of configure that the build system starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:39
msgid ""
":manual:`ctest(1)`, for the CMake language code that it runs itself, such as "
"``CTestTestfile.cmake`` files and :ref:`Dashboard Client` scripts. To record "
"coverage for each test instead, use the ``CMAKE`` value of the "
"CTest :ref:`CoverageTool <ctest-CoverageTool>` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:43
msgid ""
":manual:`cpack(1)`, for the CPack configuration file, the CPack generator "
"modules and the install scripts that it runs to make a package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:46
msgid "These modes do not record coverage and do not check the directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:48
msgid ":manual:`ccmake(1)` and :manual:`cmake-gui(1)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:49
msgid ""
":option:`cmake --build` and the :option:`cmake -E` commands.  This includes "
"``cmake -E cmake_depends``, which reads files that CMake generates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:52
msgid ""
":option:`cmake --help`, :option:`cmake --version`, :option:`ctest --"
"help`, :option:`ctest --version`, :option:`cpack --help` and :option:`cpack "
"--version`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:55
msgid "``cmake --system-information``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:56
msgid ""
"``cmake --check-build-system``, which the build system runs to check whether "
"it must re-run configure.  If the check decides to re-run configure, "
"coverage starts at that point and the re-run records as usual. The "
"``PreLoad.cmake`` file that CMake reads before the check is not recorded in "
"that run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:61
msgid ""
"The compile and link launchers that :module:`CTestUseLaunchers` enables, "
"which read a file that CMake generates, once for each compile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:64
msgid ""
"Some other modes that run no CMake language code, such as ``cmake -N`` "
"and :option:`cmake --list-presets`, check the directory at startup, but "
"write no file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:69
msgid "Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:71
msgid ""
"Before it runs any CMake language code, CMake makes sure that it can write "
"files in the directory.  If the value is a relative path, or if CMake cannot "
"create the directory or write there, CMake reports an error and stops.  A "
"failure to write the file at exit does not change the exit code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:77
msgid "What Gets Recorded"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:79
msgid ""
"Each file that CMake reads as a listfile gets a record, with the absolute "
"path that CMake used to read it.  This includes files "
"under :variable:`CMAKE_ROOT` and files that CMake generates in the build "
"tree. Records can name generated files that CMake deletes later, such as the "
"projects that :command:`try_compile` configures, so report tools may need to "
"filter them out.  The CTest ``CMAKE`` :ref:`coverage tool <ctest-"
"CoverageTool>` leaves out the files under the build tree when it merges the "
"files of a test, except for an in-source build.  Files that CMake never "
"reads do not appear.  A file with no line that can count and no function or "
"macro, such as a file with only comments, gets no record, and a process that "
"has no record writes no file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:91
msgid "Lines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:93
msgid ""
"A command counts on the line where it starts, once each time it runs, even "
"if its arguments span several lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:95
msgid ""
"Opening commands such "
"as :command:`if`, :command:`foreach`, :command:`while`, :command:`block`, :command:`function` "
"and :command:`macro` count like any other command.  A :command:`while` "
"command counts once each time the loop starts, not once for each evaluation "
"of its condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:100
msgid "An :command:`elseif` counts each time CMake evaluates its condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:101
msgid ""
":command:`else` and the commands that close a block, such "
"as :command:`endif` and :command:`endfunction`, do not count.  Comments and "
"blank lines do not count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:104
msgid ""
"A command in the body of a function or macro counts each time the body runs, "
"on its line in the file that defines the function or macro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:106
msgid ""
"A deferred call made with :command:`cmake_language(DEFER)` counts on its own "
"line when it runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:108
msgid ""
"A command that CMake skips because of an earlier fatal error does not count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:110
msgid ""
"A command that another command runs on the same line does not add a hit. "
"Examples are the command that :command:`cmake_language(CALL)` runs, and the "
"commands that :command:`list` operations call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:113
msgid ""
"Code that :command:`cmake_language(EVAL CODE) <cmake_language(EVAL)>` runs "
"is left out, because it has no file.  The :command:`cmake_language` line "
"itself counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:116
msgid ""
"Each line that can count appears in the record, with zero hits if it never "
"ran."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:119
msgid "Functions and macros:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:121
msgid ""
"Each :command:`function` and :command:`macro` definition gets one function "
"record, with the name as written in the source and the line of the "
"definition.  Its count is the number of calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:124
msgid ""
"If one file defines the same name more than once, each definition gets its "
"own record, named ``<name>@<line>``, for example ``foo@120`` and "
"``foo@135``.  A name that one file defines once keeps its name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:127
msgid ""
"A name is percent-encoded as in URLs: ``%`` is written as ``%25``, a comma "
"as ``%2C``, a line break as ``%0A`` or ``%0D``, and ``@`` as ``%40``.  Other "
"characters are written as they are.  For example, a function named ``a,b`` "
"is written as ``a%2Cb``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:131
msgid ""
"When CMake reads a tracefile back, it removes the ``@<line>`` suffix and "
"decodes the name, so every name reads back as written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:135
msgid "Output Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CMAKE_LISTFILE_COVERAGE_DIR.rst:137
msgid ""
"Each process that records coverage writes one lcov tracefile, named ``<pid>-"
"<token>.info``, where ``<pid>`` is the process ID and ``<token>`` is a "
"random value.  The file uses the ``SF``, ``FN``, ``FNDA``, ``FNF``, ``FNH``, "
"``DA``, ``LF`` and ``LH`` records.  CMake never deletes or merges files in "
"the directory.  Clear the directory before a new run."
msgstr ""
